{ "Identifier":           {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "CAE-ASE-V1.0-I01", "AIMName": "1CAE-ASE-V1.0-I01"},
  "Header":               "CAE-ASE-V1.0",

  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Description":          "Audio Scene Editing. One Basic Audio Scene is open at a time, so a User Command need not name it: a Basic Audio Scene arriving is opened, and the first Object added to no open Scene creates one. The User Command places Basic Audio Objects - named by their identifiers in Shared Storage - (AddedObjects), moves them (MovedObjects), changes where they are (ChangedObjects), takes them out (RemovedObjects) and sets where the Scene is heard from (UserPoV, also on its own Port). Every edit is a new version in Shared Storage. Outputs: the open Basic Audio Scene, and the User Command, with its report half (UserCommandReport) saying how each action was executed.",

  "InternalTypes":        [],

